    "function": "Shows esterase activity, with a preference for short- and medium-chain fatty acids. Also has weak lipase activity, but does not exhibit cutinase activity. Hydrolyzes various p-nitrophenol-linked aliphatic esters, including pNP-butyrate (C4), pNP-valerate (C5), pNP-hexanoate (C6), pNP-octanoate (C8) and pNP-decanoate (C10). Can use pNP-laurate (C12) and pNP-myristate (C14), with lower efficiency. Can also hydrolyze monocaprylin and triolein, with a slow turnover..; FUNCTION: Induces a strong delayed-type hypersensitivity (DTH) response in animal model of tuberculosis, cellular and humoral immun",
